  "routeAdjustment": "Native minimal-polynomial divisibility, roots and the degree-one criterion replace the external polynomial gcd construction. Existing actual prime products supply splitting and distinctness. The common-root phase is identified directly, without an unnecessary finite-index congruence calculation. All field objects are the original Laurent subfields and their native inclusion maps.",
  "discharged": "Native relative-degree multiplicativity and existing Dedekind-psi formulas derive the relative prime-step degree p or p+1 from explicit induction degree and generation. Primitive-index arithmetic, actual Laurent leading terms and primitive-root injectivity exclude every twice-expanded preceding-level conjugate. Actual field embeddings send contained j substitutions to their expanded minimal-polynomial roots; the lower product identity derives the preceding root shape and discharges the removed-root distinction. Strong induction then constructs every indexed root and proves the exact original expanded minimal polynomial equals the primitive triangular product over an algebraically closed characteristic-zero coefficient field, under generation and degree at divisor levels.",
  "remaining": "The joint all-level induction must still prove generation and degree; the new conditional product identity is to be used only on proper divisors in that induction. Composite generation and degree, modular ramification and fiber counts, numerical genus, analytic cusp-form realization and the period/arithmetic/symmetric-power gates remain required. DUB-17--20 OPEN; 16/20. No acceptance gate closes here.",
